      <h1 class="custom-main-title">A master catalog of pomological datasets, propagation assets, and regional research engines.</h1>
      
      <p style="margin-bottom: 32px;">To successfully cultivate rare fruit across northern California’s microclimates, structured knowledge is essential. Below is our complete archive of recommended platforms, compatibility spreadsheets, and regional diagnostic tools to optimize your home orchard performance.</p>

      <!-- ==================== CATEGORY 1 ==================== -->
      <h2>🌐 Central CRFG Ecosystem Foundations</h2>
      <p class="category-intro">The core data repositories managed by our parent organization form the operational base for fruit propagation and registration in California.</p>
      
      <div class="resource-grid">
        <a href="https://crfg.org" target="_blank" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>CRFG Parent Organization Portal</h3>
            <p>Access the definitive state-level database containing structural announcements, registered seed-banking registries, statewide conventions, and formal pomological updates.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">Visit crfg.org <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>

        <a href="https://crfg.org/publications/fruit-facts/" target="_blank" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>CRFG Official Fruit Facts</h3>
            <p>A comprehensive cultural reference encyclopedia detailing botanical origins, structural soil profiles, hydration parameters, and cold thresholds for dozens of rare varieties.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">Browse Fruit Facts <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>

        <a href="https://crfg.org/publications/fruit-gardener/" target="_blank" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>Fruit Gardener Magazine Archives</h3>
            <p>Explore centuries of aggregated cultivation wisdom, specialized grower profiles, and deep-dive varietal trial summaries across historical bi-monthly publications.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">View Archives <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== CATEGORY 2 ==================== -->
      <h2>✂️ Grafting, Scionwood & Propagation Assets</h2>
      <p class="category-intro">Essential field guidelines and alignment metrics designed to help you prepare your cuts before participating in our annual winter exchanges.</p>

      <div class="resource-grid">
        <a href="gg-scionexchange.html" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>Scionwood Collection Guidelines</h3>
            <p>Master the exact parameters for choosing dynamic vegetative wood from last season's dormant growth. Covers storage, humidity protection, and sorting practices.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">Read Collection Guide <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>

        <a href="member-guides.html" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>Stone Fruit Rootstock Compatibility</h3>
            <p>Our localized master matrix assessing structural cross-grafting boundaries, vigor behaviors, and failure vulnerabilities across plum, peach, cherry, and apricot stocks.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">View Compatibility Matrix <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>

        <a href="meetings.html" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>Graham Stott’s Grafting Class Media</h3>
            <p>Review step-by-step documentation, splice dynamics, whip-and-tongue metrics, and structural training protocols demonstrated in Graham's seasonal field labs.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">View Class Assets <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== CATEGORY 3 ==================== -->
      <h2>📈 Variety Databases & Microclimate Mapping</h2>
      <p class="category-intro">Data tracking projects designed to align localized thermal cycles with appropriate chill requirements and varietal pollination windows.</p>

      <div class="resource-grid">
        <a href="bay-area-zone-favorites.html" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>Self-Pollinating Fruit Tree Registries</h3>
            <p>A specific indexing of solo-fruiting cultivars optimized for restricted urban footprint environments, eliminating the dependency on separate tracking partners.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">Browse Self-Fruitful List <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>

        <a href="https://fruitsandnuts.ucdavis.edu/" target="_blank" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>UC Davis Fruit & Nut Research Center</h3>
            <p>The academic gold standard for regional chill hour accumulation logs, precise phenology models, and deep scientific trial results for California growers.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">Explore UC Davis Portal <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>

        <a href="where-to-buy.html" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>Bay Area Microclimate Matrix</h3>
            <p>Compare thermal margins between the foggy coastal perimeters, marine pockets, and the warm interior foothills of the Diablo Valley to ensure variety survival.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">Analyze Climate Zones <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== CATEGORY 4 ==================== -->
      <h2>🛡️ Field Diagnostics, Soil & Integrated Pest Management</h2>
      <p class="category-intro">Academic tools to defend your collection against environmental stress, physiological imbalances, and seasonal vector infestations.</p>

      <div class="resource-grid">
        <a href="https://ipm.ucanr.edu/" target="_blank" class="resource-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <h3>UC IPM Online Diagnostics Engine</h3>
            <p>The comprehensive biological reference catalog to identify codling moth cycles, peach leaf curl variables, bacterial canker, and custom cultural controls.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="card-link-label">Launch IPM Engine <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>

        <a href="online-community.html" class="resource-card">
